<title>SWITZERLAND: CYCLING-TOUR OF ROMANDIE FIFTH STAGE RESULTS.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-TOUR OF ROMANDIE FIFTH STAGE RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>NYON, Switzerland 1997-05-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading placings in the</p>
<p>69.3 kilometre fifth stage of Tour of Romandie on Sunday (second</p>
<p>half of stage this afternoon):</p>
<p>1. Mario Cipollini (Italy) one hour 31 minutes and 47 seconds</p>
<p>2. Adriano Baffi (Italy)</p>
<p>3. Mario Manzoni (Italy)</p>
<p>4. Fabio Baldato (Italy)</p>
<p>5. Gabriele Missaglia (Italy)</p>
<p>6. Filippo Casagrande (Italy)</p>
<p>7. Gian-Matteo Fagnini (Italy)</p>
<p>8. Scott Sunderland (Australia)</p>
<p>9. Andrea Noe (Italy)</p>
<p>10. Erik Dekker (Italy) all same time as winner</p>
<p>Overall leading placings:</p>
<p>1. Pavel Tonkov (Russia) 19 hours  57 minutes and 41 seconds</p>
<p> 2. Giuseppe Guerini (Italy)	   27 seconds behind</p>
<p> 3. Davide Rebellin (Italy)	    51</p>
<p> 4. Beat Zberg (Switzerland)	   55</p>
<p> 5. Gilberto Simoni (Italy)	  1:09</p>
<p>6. Alexandre Chefer (Kazakhstan)  1:19</p>
<p>7. Andrei Teteriouk (Kazakhstan)  1:20</p>
<p> 8. Chris Boardman (Britain)	 1:40</p>
<p>9. Peter Meinert-Nielsen (Denmark) 1:49</p>
<p> 10. Giuseppe Di Grande (Italy)    same time</p>
